title: Door3A
---
// Talk target of Samantha's door (Hotspots layer). It opens with the actions here: a
// popup when several are available, the only one at once. Each picks by the story graph:
// can() for the step it performs, in_box() and is_done() for what to say when it can't yet.
-> Knock <<if can("R1MoveIn", "keys")>>
    <<next_scene Route1MoveInKeys>>
-> Knock <<if in_box("R1Breakfast") and not is_done("R1Breakfast", "door")>>
    <<if can("R1Breakfast", "door")>>
        <<next_scene Route1Croissant>>
    <<elseif not is_done("R1Breakfast", "text")>>
        You: My phone's buzzing. Her, probably. Read it first.
    <<else>>
        // Behind her door.
        {$samantha_name}: ...Where's my croissant?
    <<endif>>
-> Knock <<if in_box("R1Dinner1") and not is_done("R1Dinner1", "door")>>
    <<if can("R1Dinner1", "door")>>
        <<next_scene Route1Thu1Door>>
    <<else>>
        You: She texted. I should read it first.
    <<endif>>
-> Knock <<if in_box("R1Dinner2") and not $r1_thu2_knocked>>
    <<if not is_done("R1Dinner2", "text")>>
        You: Her text first.
    <<elseif $item_wine_fox>>
        <<next_scene Route1Thu2Door>>
    <<elseif $item_wine_reserve>>
        You: The gold label. She said not that one.
    <<elseif $item_wine_house>>
        You: The house red. She'd know.
    <<else>>
        You: Empty-handed? Bring what she'd want. The shop's downstairs.
    <<endif>>
-> Take my shoes off <<if in_box("R1Dinner2") and $r1_thu2_knocked and not is_done("R1Dinner2", "door")>>
    <<next_scene Route1Thu2Shoes>>
-> Look
    <<if in_box("R1Viewing")>>
        You: Not this one. The listing said 3B.
    <<else>>
        You: 3A. Her door. The doormat doesn't say welcome.
    <<endif>>
===
